Project Update: Phase 1 & Core Backend Integrated!

Current Status:
We’ve officially wrapped up Phase 1 and fully integrated the core backend! The user session logic and communication layers are 100% operational, tested, and bug-free. The codebase has been cleaned up, organized, and fully documented in the `README.md`. We are now completely ready to kick off the next dev cycle: dynamic recipe rendering and AJAX/JS search filters.

Here is a breakdown of what we’ve built and completed so far:

---

1. UI/UX & Frontend Layout

Responsive Home Page (`index.php`):** Structured from scratch using the Bootstrap 5 grid system to make sure it looks great and scales perfectly across mobile, tablet, and desktop viewports.
Branding Assets:** Fixed and seamlessly integrated our high-res SVG brand identity (`logo.svg`) directly into the main navigation bar and the center hero section.
Design Consistency:** Standardized a clean navbar component and uniform footers across all active pages for a seamless user experience.

2. Database Architecture (`veganfood_db`)

Local Environment Setup:** Configured our relational MySQL database locally using XAMPP and phpMyAdmin.
Form Analytics:** Structured and deployed the `contact_queries` table schema to store incoming feedback securely.
User Management:** Created and verified the `users` table structure to prep for user authentication and access controls.

3. Backend & Core Server Logic

Central Configuration (`config.php`):** Initialized global system settings and established secure connection handling with the MySQL server.
Secure Feedback Portal (`contact.php`):** Built out a working contact form complete with input sanitization to safely pass user messages into the database.
Authentication Flow (`login.php` & `logout.php`):** Deployed a functional login/logout system powered by native PHP `$_SESSION` management.
Dynamic Navbar Toggles:** Programmed the navigation bar to adapt automatically—displaying a "Login" button for guests, or a personalized "Hi, [Name]" welcome alongside a "Logout" button once an active user logs in.
